    .{ .slug = "css-cursor", .title = "cursor", .category = "CSS", .search = "cursor css-cursor pointer, mouse, touch accessibility CSS", .description = "The cursor CSS property sets the mouse cursor, if any, to show when the mouse pointer is over an element.", .notes = "Cursor appearance on Android mobile devices depends on external pointer device/mouse. Cursor on iOS mobile devices also requires assistive touch to be enabled, and does not appear to respond to content.", .tested = "2025-07-02", .summary = .{ "Partial (#1) on macOS; No (#3) on iOS", "No (#2)", "Unknown on Windows, Windows Mail; No on macOS, Outlook.com, Android; No (#3) on iOS", "Partial (#4) on Desktop Webmail, Android; No (#3) on iOS" }, .clients = "Apple Mail\nmacOS: 15: Partial (#1).\niOS: 15: No (#3).\n#1: Partial. URL is not supported.\n#3: iOS assistive touch does not respond to cursor.\nGmail\nDesktop Webmail: 2025-07: No (#2).\niOS: 2025-07: No (#2).\nAndroid: 2025-07: No (#2).\nMobile Webmail: 2025-07: No (#2).\n#2: Cursor property is removed.\nOutlook\nWindows: 2007–2019: Unknown.\nWindows Mail: 2025-07: Unknown.\nmacOS: 16.98: No.\nOutlook.com: 2025-07: No.\niOS: 2025-07: No (#3).\nAndroid: 2025-07: No.\n#3: iOS assistive touch does not respond to cursor.\nYahoo! Mail\nDesktop Webmail: 2025-07: Partial (#4).\niOS: 2025-07: No (#3).\nAndroid: 2025-07: Partial (#4).\n#3: iOS assistive touch does not respond to cursor.\n#4: Partial. Only supports: crosshair, help, move, pointer, progress, text, wait, auto, default, and all single-direction resize properties.\n1&1\nDesktop Webmail: 2025-07: Unknown.\nAndroid: 2025-07: Unknown.\nAOL\nDesktop Webmail: 2025-07: Unknown.\niOS: 2025-07: Unknown.\nAndroid: 2025-07: Unknown.\nFastmail\nDesktop Webmail: 2025-07: Unknown.\nFree.fr\nDesktop Webmail: 2025-07: Unknown.\nGMX\nDesktop Webmail: 2025-07: Partial (#6).\niOS: 2025-07: No (#3).\nAndroid: 2025-07: Supported.\n#3: iOS assistive touch does not respond to cursor.\n#6: Partial. Inline CSS only. Onl